{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 52, :comments ["<b>For from a distance you shall see the land.</b> It does not say 'the land of Canaan' as it mentioned above, וראה את ארץ כנען, for the word הארץ embraces the land of Israel and the land of the living, and the Jerusalem below and the Jerusalem above. And likewise the word תראה embraces seeing with the physical eye and seeing with the eye of the intellect, for He showed him with the eye of the intellect the land that is מנגד — that is to say, which lies opposite the land of Canaan. Therefore it appears to me to explain that this is why it was necessary to repeat and say אל הארץ אשר אני נותן לבני ישראל, and it was not sufficient for him in what he said, ושמה לא תבא, to indicate that He withheld him only from the land of Israel, not from the land of the living. And likewise in the section of Pinchas Scripture mentioned in it two sightings, for it said (Numbers 27:12) וראה את הארץ and repeated וראיתה אותה — that is, depicted above; and there I have discussed it. And this land is the rank of the righteous, as David, peace be upon him, said (Psalms 116:9): אתהלך לפני ה׳ בארצות החיים, and likewise Hezekiah said (Isaiah 38:11): אמרתי לא אראה יה יה בארץ החיים." "<b>And what</b> we say on Rosh HaShanah and on Yom HaKippurim — 'Remember us for life' and 'Write us in the book of life' — the intent is upon the life of the body in this world, through which a person merits the life of the soul, which David called ארצות החיים, prepared for all Israel. This is what the Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded: 'All Israel have a share in the world to come,' as it is said (Isaiah 60:21): ועמך כלם צדיקים לעולם יירשו ארץ, and likewise it says (ibid. 57): והחוסה בי ינחל ארץ ויירש הר קדשי."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:53:44.452648974Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}